course: dictionary
lesson: 12598
title: Disciplinary and the words around it
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Disciplinary comes from discipline, which means rules and the training that keeps people following them. Disciplinary means to do with punishing people who break rules. Look for clues in the sentence, such as rules, breaking them, or a punishment.
explain: «The head teacher took disciplinary action after the fight.» The clues are fight and action. A fight breaks the rules, so disciplinary action must be a punishment. Test your meaning: put punishment in place of disciplinary and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word has a second, formal meaning too. «Interdisciplinary» means mixing two or more subjects of study, such as maths and art. The start of the word helps: inter means between, so interdisciplinary means between subjects.
explain: Words that go together give clues. A disciplinary hearing is a meeting to decide whether someone broke the rules, and a disciplinary record is a list of those past problems. Hearing, record and action all point to rules and punishment. When you are unsure, check a dictionary.
fact: Disciplinary means to do with punishing people who break rules.
fact: It can describe school, work or sport.
fact: «Disciplinary action» means a punishment, such as detention or exclusion.
fact: «Disciplinary record» means a written list of rule-breaking and the punishments given.
fact: In formal writing, «interdisciplinary» means combining more than one subject of study.
exercise: «The footballer faced a disciplinary hearing after the red card.» What is a disciplinary hearing? | A rest for tired players | A party to celebrate a win | A training session before the match | *A meeting to decide what punishment a rule-breaker should get
exercise: «The school sent a letter about disciplinary action.» Which word means to do with punishing rule-breakers? | school | letter | sent | *disciplinary
exercise: A school project that joins maths and art together is called what? | *Interdisciplinary | Disciplined | Dishonest | Unpunctual
test: «Her disciplinary record shows three warnings for being late.» What does disciplinary record mean? | A certificate for winning a race | *A written list of rule-breaking and the punishments given | A map of the school | A list of favourite songs
test: «Mixing science and history in one lesson is interdisciplinary.» What does interdisciplinary mean here? | *Using more than one subject together | Using only one subject | Working in complete silence | Breaking the rules in class
exam: «The referee's disciplinary decision stopped the player from playing next week.» What does disciplinary mean in this sentence? | Happy and playful | About cooking food | *To do with punishing a rule-breaker | Very old and worn
